description: Security and tenant-isolation rules for AutoWave (release-blocking)
alwaysApply: true
---

# Security

- Tenant isolation is release-blocking. Derive tenant from domain/auth membership; never from request input.

```php
// ❌ BAD
Lead::where('tenant_id', $request->input('tenant_id'))->get();

// ✅ GOOD — tenant scope applied by TenantContext/global scope
Lead::query()->latest()->paginate();
```

- Authorize every action server-side with Policies/Gates using granular permissions (`leads.assign`).
- Validate every input with Form Requests. Client-side validation is only UX.
- Route model binding for tenant-owned models must resolve within the current tenant (404 otherwise).
- Rate limit auth, password reset, public forms and webhooks.
- Verify webhook signatures before parsing payloads; reject replays where the provider supports it.
- Uploads: validate size, MIME, extension; store under `tenant/{tenant_id}/...`; serve private files via signed/authorized routes.
- Never send secrets, API keys, tokens or password hashes to the browser (Inertia props, JS bundles, logs).
- Secrets live only in `.env` / server environment. Never commit `.env`.
- Log security events and sensitive admin actions to the audit log with tenant_id, user_id, IP.
- Super Admin routes live only on the admin domain and require platform-admin authorization.
